#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: sunless sea!
#> pause: 40
#> must: Down to a sunless sea!
#> must: A stately pleasure dome decree:
#> not: In Xanadu
#> not: sunless sea.
#> source: $s/
# 4. Line-number addresses, and $ for the last line. McMahon 2.1
# A line number counts input lines (across all input files; it never resets).
# "1d" deletes line 1. "$" is the special address for the last line: here
# "$s/\.$/!/" swaps the final period for an exclamation mark on that line only
# (the \. means a literal dot; a bare . would match any character).
# Try: change 1d to 3d, or $s to 2s.
1d
$s/\.$/!/

#DATA
In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
A stately pleasure dome decree:
Where Alph, the sacred river, ran
Through caverns measureless to man
Down to a sunless sea.
